      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the distance traveled by the tip of the second hand during a 30-minute period, we need to calculate the circumference of the circle traced by the tip of the second hand and then find out how much of this circumference is covered in 30 minutes.\n\n1. **Determine the Circumference of the Circle:**\n   The second hand moves in a circle with a radius of 6 cm. The formula for the circumference \\( C \\) of a circle is given by:\n   \\[\n   C = 2 \\pi r\n   \\]\n   where \\( r \\) is the radius of the circle. Substituting the given radius:\n   \\[\n   C = 2 \\pi \\times 6 = 12 \\pi \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the Distance Covered in 30 Minutes:**\n   The second hand completes one full revolution every 60 seconds (1 minute). Therefore, in 30 minutes, the second hand completes half of its full revolution because:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{30 \\text{ minutes}}{1 \\text{ minute}} = 30 \\text{ half-revolutions}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the Total Distance Traveled:**\n   Since the second hand covers \\( 12 \\pi \\) cm in one full revolution, in 30 half-revolutions, the distance traveled is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Distance} = 30 \\times 12 \\pi = 360 \\pi \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the distance traveled by the tip of the second hand during a 30-minute period is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{360\\pi}\n\\]",
