      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to calculate the distance traveled by the tip of the second hand during a period of 30 minutes. The second hand completes one full revolution every 60 seconds, and since 30 minutes is equivalent to 1800 seconds, we need to determine how many full revolutions the second hand completes in 1800 seconds.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the circumference of the circle traced by the tip of the second hand. The radius of the circle is 6 cm, so the circumference \\( C \\) is given by the formula:\n\\[\nC = 2 \\pi r = 2 \\pi \\times 6 = 12 \\pi \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find out how many full revolutions the second hand completes in 1800 seconds. Since the second hand completes one full revolution every 60 seconds, in 1800 seconds it will complete:\n\\[\n\\frac{1800}{60} = 30 \\text{ revolutions}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total distance traveled by the tip of the second hand in 30 minutes is the product of the circumference of the circle and the number of revolutions:\n\\[\n30 \\times 12 \\pi = 360 \\pi \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nSo, the distance traveled by the tip of the second hand during a period of 30 minutes is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{360\\pi}\n\\]",
